 401               /TTYGCH:       GETS A CHAR FROM KBD
 402               /       IF GOT ^Z, IT SETS TTYEOF FLAG
 403               /       LEAVES IT IN AC IN 7-BIT
 404               
 405               /TTYPRT:        PRINTS CHAR IN AC ON TTY
 406               /       IGNORES NULLS
 407               /       PRINTS ^X ON CONTROL CHARS (EXCEPT CR, LF, FF, VT, TAB)
 408               /       PRINTS 'X ON LOWER CASE
 409               
 410               /HANDLES TABS CORRECTLY
 411               /       AND AUTOMATICALLY PRINTS CR/LF AT EOL
 412               /       PRINTS ESCAPE AS $
 413               
 414               /TTYTLS:        USED TO ACTUALLY PRINT CHAR
 415               /               IT HANDLES TABS AUTOMATICALLY
 416               /               AND CR/LF'S AT END OF LINE
 417               
 418               /TTYPCH:        IT USES TTYPRT TO PRINT CHAR BUT ALSO RESPONDS TO
 419               /               ^C, ^O, ^S, ^Q.
 420               /               IF ^Z IS BEING PRINTED, IT THEN STOPS FURTHER PRINTING
 421               /MUST BE AT TOP OF PAGE
